---
// Shipping & Returns — §4.7: "mirror Etsy policy exactly; contradictions
// cause disputes." This mirrors Saida's real Etsy shop policy. Every order
// still fulfills through Etsy (§1.1 — catalog-first, Etsy-fulfilled), so
// this page describes how that process works rather than implying the
// site itself handles shipping or returns.
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  seoTitle="Shipping & Returns — Meros Silkworks"
  seoDescription="Shipping, delivery estimates, and return policy for Meros Silkworks orders placed through Etsy."
  title="Shipping & Returns"
>
  <p>
    Every order here is placed and fulfilled through our Etsy shop, so the policies below are
    exactly what applies at checkout on Etsy — nothing on this page overrides or differs from it.
  </p>

  <h2>Shipping</h2>
  <p>Orders ship from Hamburg, NJ. Shipping a shorter distance is kinder to the planet, so we ship as locally as we can.</p>
  <p>
    Standard shipping is a flat rate of around $5.40 per item on most listings. The neck scarf and
    vest ship free, given their higher value and weight. Any order totaling $35 or more ships free
    shop-wide, regardless of what's in it.
  </p>
  <p>Delivery typically takes about 1–2 weeks from when the order is placed.</p>

  <h2>Returns &amp; Exchanges</h2>
  <p>Return and exchange terms depend on what you've ordered — they aren't the same across the whole shop.</p>
  <p>
    <strong>Small, everyday accessories</strong> — hair ties, scrunchies, earrings, the hair bow,
    the bag charm/ribbon, and the hat — can be exchanged within 14 days. The buyer covers return
    shipping, and if the item comes back in anything less than its original condition, the buyer is
    responsible for the resulting loss in value.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>One-of-a-kind larger pieces</strong> — the neck scarf, the vest, and by extension the
    custom Baska — are cut from a single, limited run of yardage, so returns and exchanges aren't
    accepted on these. If something's wrong with the order, reach out directly and it'll get sorted
    out.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    For anything not covered here — a damaged item, a question about an order in progress — message
    the shop directly through Etsy or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
